course: dictionary
lesson: 8776
title: Shady: out of the sun, or not to be trusted
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Shady describes a place where the sun cannot reach, because a tree or a building blocks the light. The place is cool and a bit dark. «She chooses the shady swings instead.» The swings are out of the sun, so shady tells you where she wants to sit.
explain: Test your guess by swapping in your meaning: «She chooses the swings out of the sun instead.» That still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. A good check always works this way.
explain: Shady has a second meaning too. When people talk about a shady deal or a shady character, they mean something dishonest or suspicious. The words around the word give you the clue, because a deal that is hidden or unfair is not like a plain sunny afternoon.
fact: Shady means out of the sun, cool and partly dark, because something blocks the light.
fact: A shady tree or plant gives shade.
fact: Ferns and moss grow best in shady places.
fact: On hot, sunny days, sit in a shady spot to avoid sunburn and heatstroke.
fact: Informally, shady means dishonest or suspicious, as in a shady deal or a shady character.
exercise: «She chooses the shady swings instead.» What does shady mean here? | Wet from the rain | Very bright and sunny | *Out of the sun, cool and partly dark | Dishonest and suspicious
exercise: «Moss can grow on any damp, shady side of a tree.» Find and copy one word that tells you the moss likes a place without sun. | moss | tree | *shady | damp
exercise: Mum says, «A shady tree gives us a cool place to sit.» What does the tree give? | Sunshine | Snow | Rain | *Shade
test: Ferns grow best in shady places, so where would you look for them? | On a bare, sunny hill | *In a shady wood, out of the sun | On a busy road at noon | In the middle of a hot desert
test: Ben says, «That was a shady deal.» What does shady mean here? | Cool and out of the sun | *Dishonest or suspicious | Shiny and new | Very sunny and bright
exam: «On hot days, sit in a shady spot to avoid sunburn.» What is a shady spot? | A place made of glass | *A place out of the sun, cool and partly dark | A place full of sunshine | A spot with lots of rain
